    "title": "Etowah's Myles commits to Clark Atlanta - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By gcallaghan ,\n13 hours ago Etowah’s William Myles drives past an Eagles Landing’s defender during a game last season. By Special — Mark He, File Etowah guard William Myles announced his commitment to Clark Atlanta on Monday, shortly before the 2025-26 high school basketball season is set to begin.\nMyles, a 5-foot-10 senior, transferred to Etowah from Lee County ahead of the 2023-24 campaign, then he helped lead the Eagles to a 23-7 overall record and 9-3 mark in Region 5 .\nFollowing the 2024-25 season, Myles was named to the all-Region 5 team, along with the all-county second team. He averaged 12 points, 6 assists and 2.5 steals alongside current Young Harris guard Cooper Heller in the Etowah backcourt.\nMyles was recruited by Clark Atlanta coach Alfred Jordan and assistant Joshua Jackson, and they extended the official offer to Myles July 15. The Etowah standout also had offers from Calhoun Community College and Reinhardt.\nClark Atlanta, a Division II program, is coming off back-to-back Southern Intercollegiate Athletic Conference Eastern Division titles after finishing 19-10 overall and 15-5 in conference play. The Panthers had two players make the preseason all-conference teams with Ny’Mire Little and Kharye Cayne.\nWith three straight winning seasons now under his belt, Jordan has built Clark Atlanta into a successful program. He was named the HBCU Division II Coach of the Year and HBCU National Coach of the Year in 2024 after leading the Panthers to a 17-win increase in just his second season.\n1",
